{
  "schema": "endfield.extend-data-spawner-library-native-contract.v2",
  "status": "validated",
  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Selected native input hashes, metadata field types and offsets, method identities, code bytes and decisive instructions.",
    "direct": "SpawnerConfigData indexes enemyLibrary by item.key. GameplayNetwork._Handle_EnemySpawnerObjectEnd copies each SPAWNER_DETAIL objId/actionId/spawnIdx into a SpawnDataDetail list and calls SpawnerManager.OnEnemySpawnerObjectEnd, which passes the list to SpawnerRuntime.SetupSpawnData and stores serverId -> actionId in m_entityId2ActionIdDict. SpawnerManager.TryGetLibraryItem uses the entity server ID to retrieve that action, reads its SpawnMonsterFromTemplateV2.libraryKey, and looks up that key in the spawner config's library dictionary. EnemyAIComponent._InitSync uses its entity server ID and parent spawner to request the item; when overrideAIConfig is nonempty and the typed asset loads, it calls EnemyAIRuntimeCfg.SetOverrideData with EnemyAIConfigDataOverride. Its TryGetRuntimeBornData branch calls _TryGetSpawnerLibraryItem and reads the selected item's bornTemplateId and bornBehaviorData as separate born-data outputs; the resolver itself delegates to TryGetLibraryItem. Separately, the EnemyServerData message constructor copies SCENE_MONSTER.commonInfo.templateid to enemyId and SCENE_MONSTER.monsterLibraryKey to subgameLibraryKey.",
    "conditional": "These are unpatched static native branches. The lookup, override, and born-data fallback require a selected spawner, an entity-to-action mapping, matching libraryKey, relevant nonempty item fields, and runtime execution. The born-data fallback is bypassed when entity-provided born data takes precedence.",
    "unresolved": "No checked instruction compares or copies SpawnerEnemyLibraryItem.enemyId to Proto.SCENE_MONSTER.commonInfo.templateid. The producer of the live monster message, selected EnemyInfo/EntityNode, and live override execution are not witnessed."
  },
